//? Title: Run-length encoding: actual raw-byte spans and logical records
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Represent repeated raw-byte spans as symbol/count records while allowing exact
reconstruction. Run-length encoding stores maximal equal-byte spans as
symbol/count records. Native scanner and append traces replace report-local
inspection logic. The original bitmap scanline and run-free alphabet remain,
with explicit embedded-byte and allocation controls.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For N source bytes and R maximal runs, each record stores a byte and a positive
count, with counts summing to N. R is a logical record count, not serialized
bytes. A format with fixed count width c would cost R*(1+c) bytes before
framing, but this API defines no such wire format. The actual scanner tests the
initial byte of every run and one failing boundary except at the last run. Thus
nonempty input causes N+R-1 equality tests. Decoding emits exactly sum(counts)
bytes. Both take time linear in actual input/output size.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/run_length_encoding_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = a::rle_encode_trace("AAABB");
    auto d = a::rle_decode_trace(t.runs);
    std::print("| run | byte code | begin | end | comparisons |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.run_index,
                   unsigned(static_cast<unsigned char>(s.symbol)), s.begin,
                   s.end, s.comparisons);
    std::print("Actual decoded text `{}`; comparisons {}.\n", d.text,
               t.comparisons);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         std::format("Actual input bytes {}", t.text.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual positive runs {}", t.runs.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual decoded bytes {}", d.emitted_bytes));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/run_length_encoding_tiny.svg");
}
```
